(5538199, 799078, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is really interesting and I like that I can see red and yellow hues - I am embracing all interpretations of ''duotone'' here and this is a nice example of one interpretation. (I do wonder about the choice of keeping the ''off-image'' white dots top right though.)</td>', 'This is really interesting and I like that I can see red and yellow hues - I am embracing all interpretations of ''duotone'' here and this is a nice example of one interpretation. (I do wonder about the choice of keeping the ''off-image'' white dots top right though.)', '2009-06-21 05:38:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5538200, 799177, 100393, '<td valign="top">Nice scene and a nearly good image - but for me this looks a little over-sharpened and a bit harsh as a consequence.</td>', 'Nice scene and a nearly good image - but for me this looks a little over-sharpened and a bit harsh as a consequence.', '2009-06-21 05:40:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5538201, 798986, 100393, '<td valign="top">Wow, excellent choice of colour for your second tone. Great clarity. I''m not sure whether it is a consequence of post-processing or just some lighter background blur but the lighter areas under the leaves look a little halo-ish - I think I might have been tempted to blend that area into the background a little more (though as the the photographer if I knew it was something in the background I''d probably leave it).</td>', 'Wow, excellent choice of colour for your second tone. Great clarity. I''m not sure whether it is a consequence of post-processing or just some lighter background blur but the lighter areas under the leaves look a little halo-ish - I think I might have been tempted to blend that area into the background a little more (though as the the photographer if I knew it was something in the background I''d probably leave it).', '2009-06-21 05:43:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5538202, 799180, 100393, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a great image - then I noticed the house top right and for me that knocks a lot of the magic out of it. I would have cropped it out and then cloned out the house in the background too (which I''m sure would have passed muster - I''ve taken out an entire power pylon with SC approval before).</td>', 'I thought this was a great image - then I noticed the house top right and for me that knocks a lot of the magic out of it. I would have cropped it out and then cloned out the house in the background too (which I''m sure would have passed muster - I''ve taken out an entire power pylon with SC approval before).', '2009-06-21 05:47:03.000000', NULL, 1),
